00:04:11,538 --> 00:04:17,538
The power of one

2
00:08:23,076 --> 00:08:29,076
Bilal: A New Breed of Hero is a animation, action,
adventure film directed by Ayman Jamal.

3
00:12:34,615 --> 00:12:40,615
A thousand years ago, one boy with a dream of becoming a great warrior is
abducted with his sister and taken to a land far away from home.

4
00:16:46,153 --> 00:16:52,153
Thrown into a world where greed and injustice rule all, Bilal finds
the courage to raise his voice and make a change.

5
00:20:57,692 --> 00:21:03,692
Inspired by true events, this is a story of a real hero who
earned his remembrance in time and history.

6
00:25:09,230 --> 00:25:15,230
Bilal (voice), played by Adewale Akinnuoye-Agbaje.

7
00:29:20,769 --> 00:29:26,769
Ghufaira (Teen) (voice), played by China Anne McClain.

8
00:33:32,307 --> 00:33:38,307
Umayya (voice), played by Ian McShane.

9
00:37:43,846 --> 00:37:49,846
Bilal (Teen) (voice), played by Jacob Latimore.

10
00:41:55,384 --> 00:42:01,384
Ghufaira / Hamama (voice), played by Cynthia Kaye McWilliams.

11
00:46:06,923 --> 00:46:12,923
Charlatan Priest (voice), played by Fred Tatasciore.

12
00:50:18,461 --> 00:50:24,461
Bilal: A New Breed of Hero is a 2015 English-language Emirati 3D animated action-adventure film about
the birth of Islam, produced by Barajoun Entertainment and co-directed by Khurram H.

13
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:36,000
Alavi and Ayman Jamal.

14
00:58:41,538 --> 00:58:47,538
With a story by Jamal, the screenplay was written by Alavi,
Alex Kronemer, Michael Wolfe and Yassin Kamel.

15
01:02:53,076 --> 01:02:59,076
With this film, Jamal aimed to depict heroes from
the history of the Arabian Peninsula.

16
01:07:04,615 --> 01:07:10,615
The film depicts the life of Bilal ibn Rabah, who, known for his beautiful voice, was
freed from slavery and rose to a position of prominence in 632 AD.

17
01:11:16,153 --> 01:11:22,153
The voice cast features Adewale Akinnuoye-Agbaje, Ian McShane, China Anne McClain, Jacob
Latimore, Thomas Ian Nicholas, Fred Tatasciore, Cynthia McWilliams, Jon Curry, Dave B.

18
01:15:27,692 --> 01:15:33,692
Mitchell and Michael Gross.

19
01:19:39,230 --> 01:19:45,230
Bilal premiered on December 9, 2015, at the 12th
Annual International Dubai Film Festival.

20
01:23:50,769 --> 01:23:56,769
Starting September 8, 2016, the film released throughout the MENA region.

21
01:28:02,307 --> 01:28:08,307
The film began an international rollout in February 2018.

22
01:32:13,846 --> 01:32:19,846
Bilal won "Best Inspiring Movie" on Animation Day
at the 2016 Cannes Film Festival.

23
01:36:25,384 --> 01:36:31,384
It won "Best Innovative Movie" at the BroadCast Pro Middle East Award 2016.

24
01:40:36,923 --> 01:40:42,923
Bilal was nominated for Best Animated Feature Film at the 2016 Asia
Pacific Screen Awards, the region's highest accolade for film.

25
01:44:48,461 --> 01:44:54,461
The film explores themes of hero, dreams, legend, freedom, greed.
